{"content":[{"c":["IDDO"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Father of Ahinadab, Solomon’s official at Mahanaim, who provisioned the royal household (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.4.14","r":"1Kgs.4.14","rawR":"1Kgs.4.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.4.14","value":"1Kgs.4.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 4:14"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Gershonite Levite, descendant of Joah and forefather of Zerah (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.21","r":"1Chr.6.21","rawR":"1Chr.6.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.21","value":"1Chr.6.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:21"},"); perhaps alternately called Adaiah in verse ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.41","r":"1Chr.6.41","rawR":"1Chr.6.41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.41","value":"1Chr.6.41"}],"t":"ref","v":"41"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Adaiah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Adaiah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Adaiah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Adaiah #2"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Zechariah’s son and the chief officer of Manasseh’s half-tribe in Gilead during David’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.27.21","r":"1Chr.27.21","rawR":"1Chr.27.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.27.21","value":"1Chr.27.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 27:21"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Prophet and seer who recorded the events of Solomon’s reign concerning Jeroboam, Nebat’s son in a book of visions (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.9.29","r":"2Chr.9.29","rawR":"2Chr.9.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.9.29","value":"2Chr.9.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 9:29"},"), Rehoboam’s acts in his genealogical records (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.12.15","r":"2Chr.12.15","rawR":"2Chr.12.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.12.15","value":"2Chr.12.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:15"},"), and Abijah’s life as part of a commentary (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.13.22","r":"2Chr.13.22","rawR":"2Chr.13.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.13.22","value":"2Chr.13.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:22"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Grandfather of Zechariah the prophet (",{"href":"?bref=Zech.1.1,7","r":"Zech.1.1,7","rawR":"Zech.1.1,7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Zech.1.1,7","value":"Zech.1.1,7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Zec 1:1, 7"},"). Iddo was a well-known priest who returned to Jerusalem from exile in 538 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},", and whose household was headed by Zechariah during Joiakim’s reign as high priest during the postexilic era (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.16","r":"Neh.12.16","rawR":"Neh.12.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.16","value":"Neh.12.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:16"},"). According to ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.5.1","r":"Ezra.5.1","rawR":"Ezra.5.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.5.1","value":"Ezra.5.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezra 5:1"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.6.14","r":"Ezra.6.14","rawR":"Ezra.6.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.6.14","value":"Ezra.6.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:14"},", Zechariah, and not Berechiah his father, was considered Iddo’s successor. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=ZechariahPerson_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"ZechariahPerson_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"ZechariahPerson_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Zechariah (Person) #20"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["6. Leading Levite at Casiphia in Babylonia to whom Ezra sent a delegation of men requesting priests and temple servants to join Ezra’s caravan returning to Palestine for service in the Jerusalem temple (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.8.17","r":"Ezra.8.17","rawR":"Ezra.8.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.8.17","value":"Ezra.8.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 8:17"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Iddo","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 4:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.4.14","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.4.14","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.4.14"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.21","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.21","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.21"},{"anchorText":"41","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.41","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.41","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.41"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 27:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.27.21","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.27.21","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.27.21"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 9:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.9.29","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.9.29","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.9.29"},{"anchorText":"12:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.12.15","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.12.15","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.12.15"},{"anchorText":"13:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.13.22","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.13.22","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.13.22"},{"anchorText":"Zec 1:1, 7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Zech.1.1,7","rawQueryValue":"Zech.1.1,7","sourceRefExact":"Zech.1.1,7"},{"anchorText":"Neh 12:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.16","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.16","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.16"},{"anchorText":"Ezra 5:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.5.1","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.5.1","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.5.1"},{"anchorText":"6:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.6.14","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.6.14","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.6.14"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 8:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.8.17","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.8.17","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.8.17"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":